target continues to change how it  operates to keep employees and customers  safe during this pandemic the huge  retailer has kept its nearly 2,000  stores open across the country and  online sales have increased more than  listen to this number 275 percent this  month chairman and CEO that's brian  cornell joins us he's outside a target  in sarasota florida good morning to you  brian grinnell really good to see you I  want to start with that huge jump in the  online shopping  were you expecting or hoping for that  kind of number and what does that tell  you about the shoppers these days well  Gail good morning and we've seen  distinct chapters throughout the  pandemic when things first started back  in February we certainly saw consumers  coming to Target to stock up on  household essentials we talked about  food and beverage growing at almost 40%  and then we've seen different behavior  along the way as people started to  shelter in place and stay at home they  were shopping for office supplies as  they were working from home and  educating their kids or games to occupy  time with their family and then clearly  as people spent more time at home and  we're getting advice to avoid being out  in public we started to see digital  sales soared in March they grew over a  hundred percent but in April growing at  over two hundred and seventy five  percent and these are just changes that  I think consumers are making right now  as they combat the virus and focus on  their own health and safety so things  like drive up behind me of just been  exploding as consumers can pull into a  target parking lot we put that order  right in there a trunk they drive away  safely and I think those are types of  services that will continue to grow over  time yeah my friend Wendy only goes to  Target Brian Cornell you'll be glad to  know that she says already you only do  self checkout and you make sure that  everybody is 6 feet apart in the store  you only let X amount of people in at  any given time said it well yeah we've  been very focused on safety first for  our team members and as we recognize we  were here to serve America during the  pandemic the first thing we started to  focus on  was a safety of our team so making sure  we're investing in our team their safety  and then obviously the safety of our  guests so we've made big investments in  our team paying benefits to make sure  that during this crisis they were well  taken care of  but importantly we've taken safety  measures for the guests so we have put  up plexiglass shields at the check Lane  as you're checking out of our stores  there's decals on the floor making sure  people provide that six feet of space  that's so necessary right now we do  meter the number of guests in our stores  at any one time so it's really about  making sure we can create a safe  shopping environment one where our  guests the target guest feels safe but  importantly where our team members feel  safe each and every day well Brian let's  talk about the team members because we  keep hearing a lot of many people on the  team are not happy they're planning to  walk off the job and they've made that  very clear what are you doing to address  their concerns well Gail I always want  to hear from our team and with over 350  thousand team members across America we  get lots of feedback each and every day  I can tell you the feedback I receive  and I heard it this morning talking to  our teams here in Sarasota they are  really proud to work for Target from the  start of this pandemic they recognize  they've been providing important  community services each and every day  allowing Americans to get those  household essentials their medication  the food and beverage they need so I  hear stories of pride and I've talked  about this throughout the pandemic the  real heroes at Target are those  frontline team workers the ones in our  supply chain and our stores every day  taking care of the American family and I  hear great stories of pride and I expect  on May 1st we'll have our teams in place  and we'll be serving America as we do  each and every day through this pandemic  I agree with you Brian those frontline  workers who are serving us every day are  also true heroes you know we all saw you  on the White House lawn last month with  other business leaders talking about  what you were planning to do to help in  this pandemic and at the time you said  that you would host drive-through  testing sites on target property so  there's one in California I believe in  the San Diego area do you have plans to  build others to set up others well Gail  we've said our parking lots are  available for testing and obviously  we've started one with the UC system in  San Diego as you might know we don't  operate our own pharmacies we've got a  great partnership with CBS  they've got pharmacists and technicians  in our stores so we've opened up our  parking lots but we don't have the  team's actually do testing so we're  looking for partners we'll certainly  make sure that our parking lots are  available for testing as we go forward  and I think we all know how important  testing is going to be as we battle this  virus  Brian Cornell thank you very much for  taking your time this morning let me  tell you I know a lot of people are glad  that you're up and running thank you  very much sir
 

